---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE_URL } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../../lib/seo';
const lang = 'en';
const code = `<iframe src="${SITE_URL}/embed/vin-decoder/" title="Free VIN decoder: specs, recalls, crash ratings and mpg" width="100%" height="1400" style="border:0;max-width:1100px" loading="lazy"></iframe>`;
---
<PageLayout title="Embed the Free VIN Decoder on Your Site, One Line of Code" description="Put the free VIN decoder on your site with one iframe line: factory specs, NHTSA recalls, NCAP crash ratings and EPA mpg, updated by the agencies themselves, no account." lang={lang} noindex={true} jsonLd={[breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', path: route('home', lang) }, { name: 'Embed the decoder', path: route('widget', lang) }])]} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Embed the decoder' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <header class="mb-6">
    <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl font-bold text-navy-900 md:text-4xl">Embed the VIN decoder</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-lg text-navy-700">One line of code puts the full decoder on your page. Results come live from NHTSA and fueleconomy.gov, so the embedded copy never goes out of date.</p>
  </header>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <p>Who uses it: credit unions on their auto loan pages, independent used-car dealers, car clubs, repair shops, driving schools and local newsrooms writing about a recall. Terms: keep the credit line under the frame visible, do not alter the results, and do not present the decoder as a vehicle history report. The frame sets no cookie and tells us nothing about your visitors. Questions: <a href={route('contact', lang)}>contact page</a>.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg bg-navy-900 p-4 text-sm text-white"><code>{code}</code></pre>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-8 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-navy-200">
    <iframe src="/embed/vin-decoder/" title="Free VIN decoder" width="100%" height="1400" style="border:0" loading="lazy"></iframe>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
